# Software and Operating Systems

<p>In Lessons 4 and 5, students shift focus to hardware and software individually, and how the two work together like a team to run a computer system. The graphic below shows how these two pieces depend on each other.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px;">
<p>📖 <b>Hardware</b> performs the physical tasks, displaying images on a screen, printing a document, storing files, or running electrical signals through circuits.</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-top: 12px;">
<p>📖 <b>Software</b> tells the hardware what to do and how to do it. It provides the instructions that guide the computer's actions, from opening an app to saving a file.</p>
</div>


<div style="width:100%; overflow-x:auto; margin:24px 0;">

  <div role="group" aria-label="Diagram showing the components of a computer system. Computer hardware includes input devices, output devices, storage devices, and internal components. Computer software includes system software, application software, and utility software." style="min-width:900px; padding:24px; box-sizing:border-box; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius:12px; box-shadow:0 2px 7px rgba(0,0,0,0.10); font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">

